      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Cohort Analysis: How does Retention evolve?"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HrH5r3wzN02L"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Granularity Level: Day of the Week\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculating the first 'DayOfWeek' for each Customer and Assigning it as his Cohort\n",
        "df['Cohort'] = df.groupby('CustomerID')['InvoiceDate'].transform('min').dt.to_period('M')\n",
        "\n",
        "# 'OrderMonth' is actually the 'DayOfWeek' of the Current Transaction\n",
        "df['OrderMonth'] = df['InvoiceDate'].dt.to_period('M')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Groupig by Cohort (First Purchase DayOfWeek) and OrderMonth (Current Transaction DayOfWeek)\n",
        "cohort = (df.groupby(['Cohort', 'OrderMonth'])['CustomerID'].nunique().reset_index()) # Then Counting Unique Customers in each Group\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculating the Period (i.e., Difference in DayOfWeek)\n",
        "cohort['Period'] = (cohort['OrderMonth'] - cohort['Cohort']).apply(lambda x: x.n)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Impact: Retention Patterns -> LTV Drivers"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "hMqaRzZRFOvV"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# The 'cohort' DataFrame provides insights into Customer Retention based on the month of their first purchase.\n",
        "# Let's break down each column:\n",
        "\n",
        "# Cohort: This column represents the 'Month' when a customer made their very first purchase.\n",
        "#         It groups customers into cohorts based on their initial engagement month (e.g., all customers\n",
        "#         who first purchased in December 2010 are in the 2010-12 Cohort).\n",
        "\n",
        "# OrderMonth: This refers to the 'Month' of the current transaction. So, for a given row, it's the month a purchase was made.\n",
        "\n",
        "# CustomerID: After the `nunique()` aggregation, this column represents the COUNT of unique customers\n",
        "#             from a specific `Cohort` (first purchase month) who made a transaction on a specific `OrderMonth` (current transaction month).\n",
        "\n",
        "# Period: This is the difference between the `OrderMonth` (current transaction month) and the `Cohort` (first purchase month).\n",
        "#         It indicates the number of 'months' that have passed since a customer's initial purchase month.\n",
        "#         For example, a 'Period' of 0 means the customer made a purchase in their cohort month.\n",
        "#         A 'Period' of 1 means they made a purchase one month after their cohort month, and so on.\n",
        "#         This column is crucial for tracking retention over time (across months).\n",
        "\n",
        "# How to interpret and use this DataFrame for analysis:\n",
        "# By analyzing the 'CustomerID' counts for different 'Periods' within each 'Cohort',\n",
        "# we can see how many customers from a given starting month (Cohort) return to make purchases\n",
        "# on subsequent months (represented by 'Period'). This helps in understanding month-based retention patterns.\n",
        "\n",
        "cohort"
      ],
