    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## Churn Analysis: Identifying Churn Risk + Retention Targets"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3l8Vg0HSUJC7"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "last = df.groupby('CustomerID')['InvoiceDate'].max()\n",
        "churn = (pd.Timestamp('2011-12-01') - last).dt.days > 90\n",
        "\n",
        "# The Latest Purchase Date for each Customer who ever Purchased, respectively, was Identified\n",
        "# Then, the Cutoff Date for this Churn Analysis was chosen as 2011-12-01\n",
        "# Subsequently, the Difference between each Customer's Last Purchase and the Cutoff Date was Calculated\n",
        "# Finally, it is checked if the Number of Days since the Last Purchase is > 90 Days before the Cutoff Date of 2011-12-01\n",
        "# \"InvoiceDate\" Series values indicates whether >90 Days have Passed [True - Inactive Customer who Churned, then] between a Customer's Last Purchase and December 12 2011 (the Cutoff Date), or Not\n",
        "\n",
        "# Basically, we are seeing if a Customer's Inactivity Period (since their last Purchase) exceeds 90 Days backwards from 2011-12-01\n",
        "\n",
        "churn"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "7fDY3oJiSRG_",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 489
        },
